message: "If you use these results or this software, please cite them as below."
title: "power-sum-graphs: Hamiltonian cycles of power-sum graphs, with certificates"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nouvier
    given-names: Frédéric
version: 1.0.0
# date-released and doi are set when the release is made and archived on Zenodo.
repository-code: "https://github.com/math-cafe/power-sum-graphs"
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC0-1.0
keywords:
  - power-sum graph
  - square-sum problem
  - Hamiltonian cycle
  - OEIS A115418
  - LKH
abstract: >-
  The least n for which the integers 1..n can be arranged in a circle with
  every two neighbours summing to a perfect k-th power is 473, 9641, 246877
  and 15748961 for k = 3, 4, 5, 6, each with a Hamiltonian cycle and a
  certificate ruling out every smaller n, and at least 587761723 for k = 7.
  Every n of the finite admissible islands of k = 4 and k = 5 is shown
  Hamiltonian. The software, posum, finds the cycles with LKH-3; two
  independent verifiers check every claim.
